{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"How do I troubleshoot DNS resolution issues in my Route 53 private hosted zone?","context":"### Confirm DNS support in the VPC\n\nTo allow private hosted zone record resolution, complete the following steps:\n\n1. Turn on DNS support in your Amazon VPC.\n2. Verify that **DNSSupport** and **DNSHostnames** are set to **True** in your VPC. For more information, see [View and update DNS attributes for your VPC](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-dns-updating.html)","url":"https://repost.aws/knowledge-center/route-53-fix-dns-resolution-private-zone"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"PrivateHostedZone | AWS CDK Reference","context":"# PrivateHostedZone L2 construct\n\nCreate a Route53 private hosted zone for use in one or more VPCs.\n\nNote that `enableDnsHostnames` and `enableDnsSupport` must have been enabled for the VPC you're configuring for private hosted zones.\n\nCloudFormation\n: `AWS::Route53::HostedZone`\n\nL1 type\n: `CfnHostedZone`\n\nSource\n: `aws-route53/lib/hosted-zone.ts`\n\nType last changed\n: v2.220.0 · 14 Oct 2025","url":"/cdk/api/v2/docs/aws-cdk-lib.aws_route53.PrivateHostedZone.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"UseDescribeVpcAttributewith a CLI","context":"#### Using AWS CLI\n\n**Example 1: To describe the enableDnsSupport attribute**\n\nThe following `describe-vpc-attribute` example describes the `enableDnsSupport` attribute. This attribute indicates whether DNS resolution is enabled for the VPC. If this attribute is `true`, the Amazon DNS server resolves DNS hostnames for your instances to their corresponding IP addresses; otherwise, it does not.\n\n```\naws ec2 describe-vpc-attribute \\\n --vpc-id vpc-0123456789abc0008 \\\n --attribute enableDnsSupport\n\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n{\n \"VpcId\": \"vpc-0123456789abc0008\",\n \"EnableDnsSupport\": {\n \"Value\": true\n }\n}\n```\n\nFor more information, see DNS attributes for your VPC in the *Amazon VPC User Guide*.\n\n**Example 2: To describe the enableDnsHostnames attribute**\n\nThe following `describe-vpc-attribute` example describes the `enableDnsHostnames` attribute. This attribute indicates whether the instances launched in the VPC get DNS hostnames. If this attribute is `true`, instances in the VPC get DNS hostnames; otherwise, they do not.\n\n```\naws ec2 describe-vpc-attribute \\\n --vpc-id vpc-0123456789abc0008 \\\n --attribute enableDnsHostnames\n\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\n{\n \"VpcId\": \"vpc-0123456789abc0008\",\n \"EnableDnsHostnames\": {\n \"Value\": true\n }\n}\n```\n\nFor more information, see DNS attributes for your VPC in the *Amazon VPC User Guide*.\n\n* For API details, see\n DescribeVpcAttribute\n in *AWS CLI Command Reference*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/code-library/latest/ug/ec2_example_ec2_DescribeVpcAttribute_section.html"}]}}

